Z||000000||DXR_DAD||09-24-2000||04:45 PM||||Well this was the weekend to lower the toy<BR>The rear was fine (Sat), today (Sun) the fronts plus replace a few other front end parts. So I got the passanger side all done <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>the driver side half way AND THEN I lost the nut for the upper ball joint!!! I've look all over.  What I need to know is, <B>What size is it?????</B> non of the parts stores have it, where else can I look.  One guy was goning to give me the nut from a new joint but it has to be ordered, I knew that!! so I'm stuck.  NEED HELP!!!!!!!!<P><BR>THANKS<BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||5
Z||000001||fiero56||09-24-2000||05:12 PM||||What I usually do when I need a nut or bolt and can't take the mate in, is go to Sear's(or similar shop), and buy all the parts that look like they might fit. Thats all I can say to help, usually get the right part the first trip even. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mattsfiero||09-24-2000||07:21 PM||||Well DRX I am currently getting ready to replace my upper passanger control arm and I will tell you that the nut size (and I checked) is a 10mm. The nut should have a machine thread (most metric do) it is also a common size. Hope this helps.<P>Matt||||reg||1
Z||000003||fieroshop||09-24-2000||07:58 PM||||Try thr FIERO SHOP in Richmond. They have it in stock.||||reg||1
Z||000004||BAM-BAM||09-24-2000||08:44 PM||||  Yo DAD, go to the parts store and look at a new MOOG ball joint, mine came with the nuts. Just size match the nut. It should be that easy, although I'll not guarentee it. Good luck<P>  Later, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT||||reg||12
