Z||000007||DXR_DAD||09-25-2000||11:14 AM||||Contra, it was a easy job!!! I did a search and got all the info I needed  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. If you just want to change the springs??? Now replacing other front end parts, that's another thing.<BR>Something should be replaced, thats just how it works. Once its all apart, replace it. Try to do it right the first time, words to live by!!!!<P><BR>PS.  KEEP ALL NUTS AND BOLTS IN A OLD CAN OR SOMETHING? THEY DO TEND TO WALK AWAY   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>DXR_DAD<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Coconut||09-25-2000||10:06 PM||||Yeah, Coconut knows all about those little nuts and bolts that have "evolved" into the walking species! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  IRRITATING to say the least! Needless to say, I've found a great use for empty coffee cans.<P>Cruisin' On, <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Coconut's_Signature_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
